1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
Gale crater, Mars. Every spacewalk has one question:

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
when do I have to turn back?

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Real NASA layers: HiRISE, THEMIS heat, slope.
Steep ground is blocked.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Targets are real outcrops on Curiosity's path.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,000
Route on foot. Return in 24 minutes.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,500
Rehearse the walk: time, oxygen and energy.

7
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,500
Oxygen down 40%? Point of no return,
then a closer target.

8
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,000
No GPS on Mars: beacons guide the way back.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Second site: Spirit's Columbia Hills. And the whole planet.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
MARS::404 — know when to turn back.
